    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d348">

                <pb facs="0541" n="469" xml:id="pg469"/>

                <head>No. 284.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hamlin to Mr. Frelinghuysen</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-05-16"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 16, 1882</date>.
                        (Received June 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 38.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your instruction No. 49,
                    relating to the order of the governor-general of the Island of Cuba, imposing on
                    and after the 1st April of this year a duty on live fish imported into the
                    island in foreign bottoms, I have now the honor to inclose herewith for your
                    information a copy of a note addressed by me on the 29th ultimo to the minister
                    of state on the subject.</p>
                <p>No reply to my note has as yet been received.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>HANNIBAL HAMLIN.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d348-a1.xml" xpointer="d348-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
